WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.212
Looking for better results from your sponsored brands campaigns?

00:00:03.212 --> 00:00:04.640
Here's a guided breakdown

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:09.120
to help you learn how to refine your targeting, increase relevant impressions, and ultimately

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:09.968
drive more clicks.

00:00:09.968 --> 00:00:13.360
By the end, you'll understand how to connect each stage of your

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:17.760
campaign to better performance and feel confident optimizing for real business results.

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:21.080
Refine targeting to help grow relevant impressions.

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:23.520
Start by reviewing keyword reports in the

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:24.286
advertising console.

00:00:24.286 --> 00:00:28.880
Focus on keywords that have driven at least five orders while maintaining

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:29.765
a healthy ROAS.

00:00:29.765 --> 00:00:33.600
For those that are new to sponsored brands or not seeing conversions yet,

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:37.920
use the Search Query Performance Report in Seller Central to identify keywords customers

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:39.909
used to find products like yours.

00:00:39.909 --> 00:00:42.560
Choose keywords with higher search query scores to

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:47.360
increase chances of conversion and don't forget to align them with a strong bidding strategy.

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:51.115
Use higher bids for exact match keywords with high conversion potential.

00:00:51.115 --> 00:00:52.480
Set moderate bids for

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:54.373
phrase match, especially branded terms.

00:00:54.373 --> 00:00:58.160
Apply lower bids for broad match to manage spend while

00:00:58.160 --> 00:00:58.972
expanding reach.

00:00:58.972 --> 00:01:03.440
Reference Amazon suggested bid ranges when setting bids, and remember low

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:08.224
impressions might mean that bids are too low or targeting is too narrow.

00:01:08.224 --> 00:01:08.960
Continuously adjust

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:13.760
based on performance data, for example, by shifting budget from underperforming to high performing

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:14.149
keywords.

00:01:14.149 --> 00:01:19.200
Use product targeting to reach customers, browsing similar items, even from other brands.

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:24.400
To keep impressions relevant and impactful, include products where offers add strong values

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:29.840
such as those with lower star ratings, fewer reviews, not eligible for prime shipping,

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:31.180
and higher price points.

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:35.200
Exclude products priced too above or below your range for better efficiency.

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:40.000
Combine keyword and product targeting strategies to improve reach and relevance.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:43.960
For better results, we recommend using both in tandem.

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:44.400
Additionally,

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:49.040
prevent unwanted impressions by creating a negative list of specific brands, products,

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:51.400
or high-cost keywords that aren't driving performance.

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:53.760
This helps ensure your ads don't appear on

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:58.560
product detail pages or search results that are unlikely to convert, helping maintain efficiency

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:00.800
while reaching the most relevant audiences.

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:02.293
Improve click-through rate.

00:02:02.293 --> 00:02:04.160
The next move is turning

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:08.880
views into clicks by aligning targeting, creative, and landing page experience for a fluid shopping

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:09.230
journey.

00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:14.480
First, align keywords with the ASINs featured in your ad and the landing page experience.

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:18.800
For a simpler approach, consider using theme targeting to help streamline this alignment.

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:23.440
Next, feature creatives that connect and test variations to find out which has more impact.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:24.720
Video or imagery?

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:27.920
Dive into those learnings for future iterations of your ads.

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:33.280
Finally, consider campaign goals and build tailored brand store sub pages that showcase

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:37.600
different product collections or structure your home page for products or categories.

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:42.240
This can help capture additional ad traffic and open up cross-marketing opportunities.

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:46.720
In both cases, ensure the products featured in your ads appear prominently on the page and

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:48.825
include interactive elements like shoppable images.

00:02:48.825 --> 00:02:51.280
Be sure to check metrics that signal

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:55.680
business growth potential like top-of-search impression share to identify opportunities

00:02:55.680 --> 00:03:00.800
for increased visibility and brand searches and detail page views in brand metrics to assess how

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:06.080
ads are supporting brand recognition and driving shoppers to search a product or brand by name.

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:11.120
Allow at least 14 days for campaigns to gather insights before making major changes.

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:14.880
This is especially important when preparing for high traffic events like Prime Day,

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:17.605
where historical trends can help inform strategy.

00:03:17.605 --> 00:03:20.720
Visit the ad console and start optimizing your

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:21.440
campaigns.
